WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.200
-I know everybody sits there,

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.267
but it would be cool
if I did this right here.

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:04.367
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.434
-Yeah, that could be the new --

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:08.634
-Too much?
-No, we can do it
that way as well.

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:10.033
It's more therapy that way.

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:11.767
-I'll go over here.
-But you look like a stud.

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:12.968
You look fantastic, by the way.
-Oh!

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.033
You know what?
-Always good to see you, J.B.

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:15.501
-You know, I love fashion

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:17.767
and I love looking good
all the time, Jimmy.

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:19.400
-I know. You do.
-I love it.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.534
I think it's a lost art.
-Fashion?

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:23.701
-Fashion! Ohh!
-Yeah.

00:00:23.701 --> 00:00:24.567
Let me just say something.

00:00:24.567 --> 00:00:26.534
I've known you for a long time.

00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:27.801
You were a writer on "SNL."

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:30.133
Very, very funny,
always nice to me.

00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:33.434
But I remember you liked comics
and you like comic books.

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:34.367
This is when like

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:35.767
-Ooh!
-no one was really --

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:37.000
I don't --

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.234
But you liked comic books

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:40.434
and would talk about it
in pitch ideas and...

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:41.701
-Mm.
-...now, you're in the

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:43.334
last two "Spider-Man."
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:44.968
-You're in like the biggest
movie of all time.

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:47.234
[ Cheering and applause ]
-It is absolutely...

00:00:47.234 --> 00:00:48.300
-You did it!

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.200
-...absolutely a blessing, man.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.434
You know what I did for it?

00:00:50.434 --> 00:00:52.334
You know what?
I sat in the audience watching

00:00:52.334 --> 00:00:54.534
an Avengers movie and I told
my wife, I said, "Baby" --

00:00:54.534 --> 00:00:55.968
I told my wife, Shah --
I said, "Baby,

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:58.868
I would love to be in the
Marvel Universe, one day"

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:00.334
And, next thing you know,
I get a phone call

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:03.734
and I'm doing an Audi commercial
with Tom Holland,

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:07.033
which was one of the sponsors
of "Far From Home," right?

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.100
And it worked out great.
We had a great time.

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.701
You know, we connected.
We laughed at the commercial.

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:13.734
Next thing you know,
a few months later,

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:15.133
they give me a call
for the movie.

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:16.501
And then, of course,

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:19.267
they brought my character back
for "No Way Home."

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:20.567
This is great!
-Mr. Dell.

00:01:20.634 --> 00:01:22.467
[ Cheering and applause ]
-Mr. Dell.

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:23.601
-How about this?

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:26.667
-[ Laughs ]
-How about this? How about this?

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:28.968
I think you do a Mr. Dell
spinoff.

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:30.067
-Oh, oh, oh.

00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:31.734
[ Cheering and applause ]
Jimmy.

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:33.067
Jimmy, don't start nothing, man.

00:01:33.067 --> 00:01:34.367
You know I love to be --
-I'm going to start something.

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:35.767
-You know I love comic books.

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:37.801
I would love to be --
The first thing I did,

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:39.868
when they called me
about doing "Spider-Man,"

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.534
the first thing you ask,
if Marvel calls you

00:01:42.534 --> 00:01:45.801
about anything is,
"What are my powers?"

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:46.901
-Yes, of course.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:48.267
-See? And they told me
I was a teacher,

00:01:48.267 --> 00:01:50.100
so I had the power of knowledge.
But it's okay.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.567
[ Laughter and applause ]
-That's good.

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:55.801
-But you know I love me
some superheroes, man.

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:58.767
I got a lot of ideas
for my own characters, you know.

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:02.067
Now, I would love
to be a character that flies,

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:03.667
but I'm a little scared
of heights, so,

00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:06.267
[ Laughter ]
I would fly two feet

00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:07.634
off the ground.

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:09.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:10.334
Just two feet, you know.

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:12.000
-Float or parallel?
-Oh, no, just --

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.267
Now, that's a good question.

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.801
If you float like this,
it's like you're riding

00:02:16.801 --> 00:02:17.834
a Segway, you know what I mean?

00:02:17.834 --> 00:02:19.167
Like this, like this.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:20.300
-Yeah.
-That ain't bad.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:22.133
-That's not bad.
-But I want to fly.

00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:24.300
I want to be able to do this
to people, say hi.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.901
And people can touch you, too.
They say, "Hey, hey,

00:02:25.901 --> 00:02:27.901
good job," see?
-Yeah.

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:29.567
[ Laughter and applause ]
You know?

00:02:29.567 --> 00:02:31.334
You can go to Starbucks.
-Yeah.

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:33.467
-You can fly by a Starbucks,
you know?

00:02:33.467 --> 00:02:35.000
Drive-throughs, you know?

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.701
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, you're only two feet
off the ground.

00:02:37.701 --> 00:02:39.000
-If I'm two feet off the ground,

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.501
I got to follow
all the traffic rules.

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:42.801
[ Laughter ]
I can't just go
through a red light.

00:02:42.801 --> 00:02:43.601
I see the light.

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:44.868
I can't just go through it.

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:46.934
I'd cause an accident.
-Yeah.

00:02:46.934 --> 00:02:48.300
How about this?
What if you're a villain?

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.033
What if you came out
as a villain?

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:51.868
-Oh, oh, well, the villain.

00:02:51.868 --> 00:02:54.834
Oh, I would be a character
called Sucker Punch.

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:57.000
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.634
And he has the gift of gab.

00:02:58.634 --> 00:03:00.067
He'll talk to you.
Next thing,

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:01.234
you get your guard down
a little bit

00:03:01.234 --> 00:03:02.067
and he'll punch you in the face.

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:03.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:06.501
Come on, man.

00:03:06.501 --> 00:03:07.934
He's a great hero.
-Sucker --

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:09.434
-Sucker Punch.

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:10.434
I got another guy.

00:03:10.434 --> 00:03:12.033
Hey, how about this hero?

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:14.801
It's a guy named What I Say?

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:17.033
[ Laughter ]
What I Say?
He has the ability to go back

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:20.534
seven seconds, resolve an issue,
you know what I mean?

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:23.968
Change his mind, then come back
to the present, see?

00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:27.234
[ Cheering and applause ]
He wins every argument.
He wins every argument.

00:03:27.234 --> 00:03:29.834
He go back seven seconds,
and then come back.

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:31.234
-[ Laughs ]
-"What I say?"

00:03:31.234 --> 00:03:32.634
-"What I say?"
-"I'll be right back."

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:33.868
Go back.

00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:36.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:38.000
[ Slapping desk ]

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.000
Aaaah!
-J.B., I got to tell you, man,

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.534
-Whoo!
-I was looking for a laugh

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:42.934
the other night, man, and I go,

00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:46.667
"Man, I forgot that 'Curb'
just wrapped the 11th season."

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:49.534
"Curb Your Enthusiasm,"
it's as funny as always.

00:03:49.534 --> 00:03:51.167
You were the funniest man
on television.

00:03:51.167 --> 00:03:52.667
-Oh, man, I appreciate it.

00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:53.734
-You were unbelievable, man.

00:03:53.734 --> 00:03:55.267
It was a great season.

00:03:55.267 --> 00:03:58.934
You are just --
You and Larry, Larry David.

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:00.934
It's just so fun to watch.

00:04:00.934 --> 00:04:02.634
I wish it was like
three hours long.

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:05.667
-I know, man.
-Do you crack him up?

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:07.167
-You know what?
As a comedian,

00:04:07.167 --> 00:04:09.634
we have great intentions
for our audience,

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:11.300
but we have bad intentions.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:12.667
We want you to wet your pants.

00:04:12.667 --> 00:04:14.234
We want you to do
all these things.

00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:16.100
When I'm performing with Larry,
I don't break.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:17.267
I don't break at all.

00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:18.634
I give him the line.

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:21.234
And my back of my mind is,
in back of my brain,

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:23.033
I'm thinking,
"I'm going to make a snot bubble

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:24.000
come out his nose."

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:25.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:25.634 --> 00:04:29.400
That's my motivation.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.901
I want to see a snot bubble.
-Come out of Larry David's nose.

00:04:31.901 --> 00:04:33.634
Want when people hold
their laughter in

00:04:33.634 --> 00:04:35.033
and you see them cracking
a little bit --

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:37.400
Because you can tell Larry's
cracking because his right

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.400
or left side of his mouth
goes like this.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.300
"Ahh!

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:43.267
[ Laughter ]
[ Mumbling ]"

00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:44.567
He does that a little bit.

00:04:44.567 --> 00:04:46.100
-That's him breaking.
-"Ahh!"

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.234
-"Ahhh!"
-He's trying to hold it in.

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:48.834
-[ Laughs ]
-But, yes,

00:04:48.834 --> 00:04:50.901
it was an amazing process, man.

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:53.534
Another thing that happened
with that --

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:55.133
I'm a seed planter, man.

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:57.901
I truly believe that, somehow,
the universe works with you

00:04:57.901 --> 00:04:59.200
in some way, man.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:01.534
When you work hard
and you put time into it, man,

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:02.934
and you love what you love --

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:04.400
You know, my wife told me
I was going to be

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.000
on "Curb Your Enthusiasm."

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.334
We would watch it.
We were actually working

00:05:08.334 --> 00:05:11.267
together at "SNL" and we would
watch "Curb," of course.

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:12.434
We'd come in,
we'd talk about "Curb"

00:05:12.434 --> 00:05:14.033
in the writers' room.

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:16.133
And I told my wife -- We were
watching the show one night.

00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:18.334
I said, "Baby, I would love
to be on this show, one day."

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:19.767
And she said, "You're going
to be on that show, one day,

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:22.367
because I could see you
and Larry together.

00:05:22.367 --> 00:05:24.033
You're both lanky as hell.

00:05:24.033 --> 00:05:26.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.133 --> 00:05:28.767
I can see you guys just working
together and laughing

00:05:28.767 --> 00:05:30.234
and doing something together."

00:05:30.234 --> 00:05:32.667
And, next thing you know, man,
I come into L.A.

00:05:32.667 --> 00:05:36.234
for a friend's memorial service,
for one day.

00:05:36.234 --> 00:05:39.100
This is after I didn't get
renewed by "SNL"

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.200
my fourth season.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.033
So I went to L.A.
for one day, man,

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:42.968
and my buddy --

00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:44.734
The Roots know my buddy,

00:05:44.734 --> 00:05:45.901
you know, Oji Pierce.

00:05:45.901 --> 00:05:47.534
He did, "This Is How We Do It."

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:48.567
"This Is How We Do It."

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:50.868
And I went in town for him
and, man,

00:05:50.868 --> 00:05:52.734
My agent sent me

00:05:52.734 --> 00:05:54.868
to "Curb Your Enthusiasm"
for an audition, man,

00:05:54.868 --> 00:05:56.067
and I walked in that room.

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:57.934
Larry was standing
in the middle of the room.

00:05:57.934 --> 00:05:59.033
You know, I have this thing I do

00:05:59.033 --> 00:06:01.801
where I come in the room
as the character.

00:06:01.801 --> 00:06:04.200
I never go in a room as J.B.
and then turn the character on

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:05.834
because I feel like
there's a disconnect.

00:06:05.834 --> 00:06:07.267
-Wow.
-I come into --

00:06:07.267 --> 00:06:08.734
I like to get the room.

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:10.801
I like to come in there and get
your attention immediately.

00:06:10.801 --> 00:06:14.200
So I came in as Leon,
had my little hand right here

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:17.000
looking around the room,
doing my little Leon thing.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.667
Larry's standing
in the middle of the room.

00:06:18.667 --> 00:06:20.901
They said, "Okay. You're gonna
improvise with Larry."

00:06:20.901 --> 00:06:22.968
I said, "Okay. Cool."

00:06:22.968 --> 00:06:24.501
And this is a character.
It's not me speaking.

00:06:24.501 --> 00:06:25.901
But I walked in the room.

00:06:25.901 --> 00:06:27.300
I said, "Okay, Larry.
Let's do this.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.300
We're gonna improvise, right?
Anything could happen.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:32.501
I might -- I might slap you
in the face. I don't know."

00:06:32.501 --> 00:06:34.367
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.367 --> 00:06:36.467
And Larry looked
at the producers like...

00:06:36.467 --> 00:06:38.467
-Who's this guy?

00:06:38.467 --> 00:06:41.300
-"Do we need to call security
on this dude?"

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.501
But -- But that was --

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:44.300
And we hit it off right away.
He laughed.

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:46.267
We laughed through
the whole audition process.

00:06:46.267 --> 00:06:47.901
We had a great time.

00:06:47.901 --> 00:06:49.367
And first day -- Quickly.

00:06:49.367 --> 00:06:51.167
First day on the job, he said

00:06:51.167 --> 00:06:53.901
it felt as though we'd been
working together for years.

00:06:53.901 --> 00:06:55.834
-Is that right?
-Yeah, because I truly believe

00:06:55.834 --> 00:06:57.467
somehow, I said, we have.

00:06:57.467 --> 00:06:58.968
I said we have.
-Yeah.

00:06:58.968 --> 00:07:01.133
-This idea came up
two years ago,

00:07:01.133 --> 00:07:02.467
somewhere two years ago.

00:07:02.467 --> 00:07:04.400
And that's the fun thing about,
you know,

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:07.133
being an actor and our journey.
We have no idea

00:07:07.133 --> 00:07:08.300
where we're going to end up at.

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:09.634
We worked together at "SNL."

00:07:09.701 --> 00:07:11.601
We worked together at "SNL."

00:07:11.601 --> 00:07:12.701
-Never knew that we would --

00:07:12.701 --> 00:07:14.567
-All younger faces, you know?

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:16.567
-Yeah, exactly. Yeah.
Younger face.

00:07:16.567 --> 00:07:18.701
-You didn't wear a suit.
You wore T-shirts all the time.

00:07:18.701 --> 00:07:20.300
-Exactly. Yeah, of course.
That's right.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:22.133
-And I believe you might have
wore shorts in the wintertime.

00:07:22.133 --> 00:07:24.834
I'm not sure.
But anyway --

00:07:24.834 --> 00:07:26.734
You were just
a young, wild dude.

00:07:26.734 --> 00:07:29.300
Look at you. Professional.
Suit, tie every night.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:30.901
Doing an amazing show like this.

00:07:30.901 --> 00:07:33.200
This is how
the journey goes, man.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:35.033
-Yeah, I'll tell you
what's great, too, is that

00:07:35.033 --> 00:07:37.267
I think the secret sauce
is we're very lucky.

00:07:37.267 --> 00:07:39.901
We have great wives.

00:07:39.901 --> 00:07:41.601
-We have great wives, man. Yes.

00:07:41.601 --> 00:07:43.467
-That's the secret sauce.
She's beautiful.

00:07:43.467 --> 00:07:48.200
-She is absolutely gorgeous,
man, and so supportive, man.

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:50.267
I cannot ask
for anything more, man.

00:07:50.267 --> 00:07:51.334
-She's the coolest.

00:07:51.334 --> 00:07:52.901
-You know, health, love,
happiness, man.

00:07:52.901 --> 00:07:56.067
It all goes together, man.
And some amazing fans, man.

00:07:56.067 --> 00:07:57.467
-That's exactly right.

00:07:57.467 --> 00:07:59.801
-And I told you --
-They're the ones.

00:07:59.801 --> 00:08:01.567
-I told you about the time
I met --

00:08:01.567 --> 00:08:03.601
I find out people
all the time are my fans.

00:08:03.601 --> 00:08:04.767
I had no idea.

00:08:04.767 --> 00:08:06.601
-Who's a fan
that you didn't have an idea?

00:08:06.601 --> 00:08:08.000
-I was in a restaurant,

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:10.534
one my favorite restaurants
called Craig's in L.A.

00:08:10.534 --> 00:08:11.767
-Yeah.

00:08:11.767 --> 00:08:13.234
-And my wife and I
are having dinner.

00:08:13.234 --> 00:08:15.067
Felt a little tap
on my shoulder.

00:08:15.067 --> 00:08:16.400
And I said, "Uh-oh."

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:19.300
And this is pre-COVID,
so I turned around.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:20.834
I was like, "Okay."

00:08:20.834 --> 00:08:22.968
-Yeah, 'cause now you wouldn't.
"Who's tapping me?"

00:08:22.968 --> 00:08:25.167
-"Give me a minute."
Put my mask back on.

00:08:25.234 --> 00:08:26.567
Put my mask back on.

00:08:26.567 --> 00:08:28.534
And someone said...

00:08:28.534 --> 00:08:30.901
"Hi. We work --

00:08:30.901 --> 00:08:33.801
We work for Mick Jagger."

00:08:33.801 --> 00:08:35.434
I said, "Oh, wow.
I love Mick Jagger."

00:08:35.434 --> 00:08:37.300
"He's a huge fan
of 'Curb Your Enthusiasm.'

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:38.868
And he loves you."

00:08:38.868 --> 00:08:41.300
I said, "What?!
I love Mick Jagger!"

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:42.434
I said, "What?!"

00:08:42.434 --> 00:08:44.601
"He's on tour right now
in Ireland.

00:08:44.601 --> 00:08:47.834
You know what? You want to --
You know what? You know what?

00:08:47.834 --> 00:08:49.701
You want to surprise him?

00:08:49.701 --> 00:08:52.734
You want to surprise him
and go to Ireland to a show?"

00:08:52.734 --> 00:08:55.567
I said, "Oh, oh.
Don't make me do this.

00:08:55.567 --> 00:08:58.767
"I've got -- I've got a show
tomorrow night in Albuquerque,

00:08:58.767 --> 00:09:03.067
but I can call and cancel,
but I can't call and cancel."

00:09:03.067 --> 00:09:05.133
They said Mick Jagger was a fan.

00:09:05.133 --> 00:09:06.801
I was blown away, man,

00:09:06.801 --> 00:09:09.400
because this dude
is the ultimate performer, man.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.067
-It's Mick Jagger.
-It's Mick Jagger, man.

00:09:11.067 --> 00:09:13.133
-He's the greatest performer.
-He's the greatest performer.

00:09:13.133 --> 00:09:14.434
And then he was in another city,

00:09:14.434 --> 00:09:17.234
and I called his assistant,
and it was after my show.

00:09:17.234 --> 00:09:19.167
It was like 12:30, 1:00
in the morning,

00:09:19.167 --> 00:09:20.534
and I called the lady back.

00:09:20.534 --> 00:09:22.300
She said,
"Call me after your show."

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:23.701
I called her after the show.

00:09:23.701 --> 00:09:27.067
She said, "Oh, I'm sorry.
He's turned in for the evening."

00:09:27.067 --> 00:09:31.000
Now, I can't see Mick Jagger
"turning in." He's so --

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:36.767
They say this man does six miles
every performance,

00:09:36.767 --> 00:09:39.667
walking back --
prancing back and forth.

00:09:39.667 --> 00:09:41.367
-Yeah.
-He does six miles!

00:09:41.367 --> 00:09:44.901
You know how --
You know how much energy

00:09:44.901 --> 00:09:47.667
you got to have to do
six miles every show?!

00:09:47.667 --> 00:09:49.901
-Yes.
-Good gracious, man.

00:09:49.901 --> 00:09:51.634
Hey. Give me a little bit.
Give me a little bit.

00:09:51.634 --> 00:09:53.434
-Yeah, yeah.
-Come on. You...

00:09:53.434 --> 00:09:54.634
♪♪

00:09:54.634 --> 00:09:56.167
-He's, like, doing that --
Yeah.

00:09:56.167 --> 00:10:01.434
♪♪

00:10:01.434 --> 00:10:03.701
Then you gotta turn in.

00:10:03.701 --> 00:10:06.467
-Oh, yeah!
-Alright!

00:10:06.467 --> 00:10:09.567
♪♪

00:10:09.567 --> 00:10:12.400
Oh, yeah!

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:15.167
Alright. Do --

00:10:15.167 --> 00:10:18.701
J.B.! J.B.! J.B.!

00:10:18.701 --> 00:10:21.334
So what did -- So what --
So what did --

00:10:21.334 --> 00:10:24.367
What did Mick say
when you talked to him?

00:10:24.367 --> 00:10:25.901
-I didn't talk to him.

00:10:25.901 --> 00:10:28.033
I didn't get a chance
to talk to the man.

00:10:28.033 --> 00:10:30.601
His assistant kept telling me...

00:10:30.601 --> 00:10:33.567
She asked me if I would
love to fly to Ireland,

00:10:33.567 --> 00:10:36.567
and I couldn't go to Ireland.
-You went to Albuquerque.

00:10:36.567 --> 00:10:39.501
You got a gig.
You're a loyal dude. That's why.

00:10:39.501 --> 00:10:43.834
But, Mick, if you're watching,
J.B. is looking to hang.

00:10:43.834 --> 00:10:47.501
-I'm looking to hang, man.
-Let's make this happen.

00:10:47.501 --> 00:10:50.834
-He would walk six miles.
We would walk six miles for you.

00:10:50.834 --> 00:10:52.567
-I will walk six miles
for you, man.

00:10:52.567 --> 00:10:54.200
I would love to meet you.

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:57.267
And I appreciate your assistant
who tried to make it work, man.

00:10:57.267 --> 00:10:59.634
But, you know, we're both
working professionals.

00:10:59.634 --> 00:11:01.701
I love you, Mick Jagger.
I love you, man.

00:11:01.701 --> 00:11:03.701
Thank you for watching
"Curb Your Enthusiasm."

00:11:03.701 --> 00:11:06.501
Thank you for supporting
J.B. Smoove and Leon.

00:11:06.501 --> 00:11:08.634
-Thank you, Mick Jagger.
-Thank you, Mick Jagger.

00:11:08.634 --> 00:11:10.667
-I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's J.B. Smoove

00:11:10.667 --> 00:11:12.267
and Larry David
in "Curb Your Enthusiasm."

00:11:12.267 --> 00:11:13.901
Take a look at this.

00:11:13.901 --> 00:11:15.234
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:11:15.234 --> 00:11:17.534
-That's why Mary Ferguson
had to go.

00:11:17.534 --> 00:11:19.901
-What are you gonna do?
You paid for the plane ticket.

00:11:19.901 --> 00:11:22.501
It's got Mary Ferguson's
name on it. It's nonrefundable.

00:11:22.501 --> 00:11:24.033
What are you gonna do? Eat it?

00:11:24.033 --> 00:11:27.000
-No, I'm-a find me
another Mary Ferguson.

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:28.868
-[ Chuckles ]
What are you talking about?

00:11:28.868 --> 00:11:30.801
-I'm gonna put an ad out.
I'm gonna get them all here.

00:11:30.801 --> 00:11:33.334
I'm gonna audition a bunch
of Mary Fergusons,

00:11:33.334 --> 00:11:35.868
find the one I like,
take her ass to Asia.

00:11:35.868 --> 00:11:38.501
-What random Mary Ferguson
is gonna go to Asia

00:11:38.501 --> 00:11:42.100
with some stranger
who's probably a sociopath?

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:44.501
-You're forgetting
one key thing here. Free.

00:11:44.501 --> 00:11:46.467
Who wouldn't want to go
to Asia for free?

00:11:46.467 --> 00:11:49.534
They'll take that chance waking
up dead for a free trip to Asia.

00:11:49.534 --> 00:11:51.067
I promise you.

00:11:51.067 --> 00:11:53.367
-I think you might
have something.

00:11:53.367 --> 00:11:55.601
-J.B. Smoove.

00:11:55.601 --> 00:11:58.067
Season 11
of "Curb Your Enthusiasm"

00:11:58.067 --> 00:12:00.133
is streaming on HBO Max.

00:12:00.133 --> 00:12:04.300
And "Spider-Man: No Way Home"
is in theaters now. J.B. Smoove!

